Street and place names over satellite; clearer locate button

Esri World Imagery carries no labels, so there was nothing to navigate by
once you zoomed in. Satellite now layers Esri World_Transportation and
World_Boundaries_and_Places over the imagery - street names, route shields
and town names, sharp to zoom 19. A switch under Base map turns them off.

The locate and drop-a-spot buttons were easy to confuse: drop-a-spot used
the classic map pin, which reads as "my location" to everyone. Find me is
now the ringed GPS dot and drop-a-spot is a pin with a plus. The map key
gained a section naming each button, since tooltips never appear on touch.

